BR_COLS = ["BR-ID", "Rule Statement", "Use Case Relevant"]
W = "Withdrawn in v27 — "
NI = " (Not implemented yet.)"
NF = " (Not fully implemented — see Code to fix.)"
BR = [
["BR-01","An account that serves only the Customer role and enters a wrong password P-17 (default 5) times in a row is locked for P-18 (default 5) minutes. An account that serves any staff role, including one that also serves the Customer role, is never locked automatically — counter machines are shared, and a wrong lock would stop a whole shift.","UC-01"],
["BR-02","When the temporary lock (BR-01) ends, the customer account unlocks and the failure counter resets to 0. A successful sign-in or a password reset through Forgot Password (UC-03) also resets the counter and clears the lock.","UC-01, UC-03"],
["BR-03","Password recovery verifies only through the registered email of the account: the user enters the email (a phone number is not accepted), and the 6-digit code is sent only to that email (GBR-15). Admin-locked or Inactive accounts cannot recover (MSG37).","UC-03"],
["BR-04","A password recovery code expires after P-15 (default 15) minutes, and the new password must be saved before that same deadline; the new password follows DBR-02.","UC-03"],
["BR-05","Withdrawn in v25 — replaced by CBR-110.","—"],
["BR-06","The system must always have at least one active Admin account."+NI,"UC-07"],
["BR-07","The last active Admin account cannot be deleted, locked or demoted, and its employee record cannot be set to Resigned."+NI,"UC-07"],
["BR-08","Only an Admin can create an Admin account or promote someone to Admin."+NI,"UC-07"],
["BR-09","The Admin can unlock a temporarily locked customer account early."+NI,"UC-07"],
["BR-10","When the Admin unlocks an account — locked manually or temporarily after failed sign-ins — a reason of 5–500 characters is required. The unlock resets the failed-attempt counter to 0 and is written to the audit log together with the reason."+NI,"UC-07"],
["BR-11","The gym's financial parameters are: package prices, VAT, PT commission rate and fees.","UC-09"],
["BR-12","The gym has one default opening and closing time for every day (P-19, 05:30–22:00); the Manager declares only the dates that differ — other hours or closed all day (OperatingHourExceptions).","UC-11"],
["BR-13","An Inactive employee no longer appears in the list of working staff.","UC-13"],
["BR-14","The Manager cannot approve a leave request if, after approval, the staff remaining in any affected shift (GBR-38) would fall below P-13 PTs or P-14 Receptionists (CBR-88, CBR-90). Every Working PT and Receptionist is assumed to work both shifts; other Pending requests are not counted, Approved ones are. Example: with exactly 2 PTs left, no PT may take leave.","UC-15"],
["BR-15","A member with no running package and no unused PT session is deleted immediately."+NF,"UC-16"],
["BR-16","The Receptionist cannot delete on their own a profile that still has a running package or unused PT sessions."+NF,"UC-16"],
["BR-17","Every deletion of a customer profile requires a reason (5–500 characters)."+NF,"UC-16"],
["BR-18","A profile cannot change between Dependent and self-owned. When a child gets their own phone number, the current package runs out, the old profile is deleted and a new self-owned profile is created."+NF,"UC-16"],
["BR-19","The Receptionist changes the phone number or email of a customer profile that has an account only when the customer is at the counter and has been checked against the check-in photo; if the profile has no check-in photo yet, the Receptionist checks an identity document and takes the check-in photo on the spot. The change applies to every role of that Person (CBR-110)."+NF,"UC-16"],
["BR-20","When the Receptionist freezes the package of an Active member, the member becomes Frozen."+NF,"UC-18"],
["BR-21","Only a membership package can be frozen; PT packages (single and couple) cannot."+NF,"UC-18"],
["BR-22","Freezing a membership package costs P-03 (default 0 = free of charge)."+NF,"UC-18"],
["BR-23","An expired package cannot be frozen. A freeze starts at the earliest tomorrow and its end date cannot be before its start date."+NF,"UC-18"],
["BR-24","A package that has used up its freeze allowance (P-01, copied into the subscription) cannot be frozen again."+NF,"UC-18"],
["BR-25","When the freeze period ends, the package reopens automatically (JOB-01) and the member returns to Active; the Receptionist does nothing.","UC-18"],
["BR-26","The Receptionist may end a freeze early: the package reopens immediately, the member returns to Active and the end date is extended only by the days actually frozen (DBR-51). The freeze allowance stays used (BR-24, P-01); sessions already closed by JOB-04 are not restored (CBR-68)."+NF,"UC-18"],
["BR-27","A customer who cannot use the gym today (no valid Membership or DayPass, or frozen — CBR-117) cannot check in; a customer holding only a PT package is refused (CBR-58).","UC-19"],
["BR-28","Check-in only needs the customer code or phone number (or a name search); no card and no login account are required.","UC-19"],
["BR-29","A day pass becomes Used as soon as the customer checks in with it.","UC-19"],
["BR-30","A day pass needs no check-in photo and no face comparison.","UC-19"],
["BR-31","When checking in a customer holding a package of one month or longer, the Receptionist compares the customer's face with the check-in photo shown on screen and confirms it.","UC-19"],
["BR-32","An unused day pass expires at the end of the day (JOB-03)."+NI,"UC-19"],
["BR-33","If a customer with a package of one month or longer has no check-in photo yet (for example after buying online), the Receptionist takes the photo at the first check-in before completing it.","UC-19"],
["BR-34","A membership package allows unlimited check-ins within its validity, including several entries on the same day. Only the day pass is limited to a single entry (CBR-36, BR-29).","UC-19"],
["BR-35","PT package sessions are generated only on Monday to Friday. The gym itself opens at the weekend like any other day: check-in, day passes, counter sales and single sessions work normally on Saturday and Sunday, and the PT may reschedule a session to a weekend slot (BR-64).","UC-21"],
["BR-36","The weekly template and the week tabs of the PT sale screen show only Monday to Friday.","UC-21"],
["BR-37","Both members of a couple package must meet CBR-59 and CBR-14 when the order is created; the partner cannot be the holder. A person with only a day pass, or with an expired or frozen membership, cannot join a couple package.","UC-21"],
["BR-38","The PT consults the customer in person before the package is sold.","UC-21"],
["BR-39","The customer chooses the PT; the PT cannot choose or refuse a customer.","UC-21"],
["BR-40","A PT package runs by term: the Receptionist picks the start date (today to today + 30 days, default tomorrow) and the system computes end date = start date + package duration, last day inclusive (GBR-03). The system generates one session for each date in the term that falls on a weekday chosen in the template (CBR-43), unless the date was overridden to \"no session\" or cannot be scheduled (BR-41). Closed days and days on which the PT has a leave request still get a session, marked amber, for the PT to reschedule (CBR-56, CBR-83). No make-up sessions, no term extension. The number of generated sessions is the number of sessions held.","UC-21"],
["BR-41","A date cannot be scheduled when: the time has passed, the customer (or partner) has another session overlapping it, the PT already has a customer then, the slot is held for another order, the PT withdrew that slot, an old slot at that time has a different length, or another slot of the PT overlaps it. The Receptionist may pick another time for that date only (including a slot the PT opened only on that date) or set no session; a date with no workable time gets no session and no make-up.","UC-21"],
["BR-42","An order can use at most one voucher.","UC-20, UC-23"],
["BR-43","When a voucher is applied successfully, its used count increases by one.","UC-23"],
["BR-44","When an order with a voucher is Cancelled for any reason (CBR-11, CBR-70, CBR-71, CBR-72), one use of the voucher is returned.","UC-23"],
["BR-45","When a customer removes a voucher from a Pending order or replaces it, one use of the old voucher is returned; an invalid new code leaves the current discount untouched.","UC-23"],
["BR-46","The Receptionist can close a shift only after entering the counted cash; if it differs from the expected cash (DBR-55), a reason is required."+NF,"UC-25"],
["BR-47","Money from transactions under CBR-72 is refunded to the customer by the Manager outside the system, then confirmed in the system (BR-83).","UC-26"],
["BR-48","Only the Receptionist closes a maintenance request (In Progress → Closed), after checking that the item has been repaired, with an acceptance note of 5–500 characters.","UC-28"],
["BR-49","Only the Manager approves (Open → In Progress) or rejects (Open → Rejected, reason 5–500 characters) a maintenance request; a request that is no longer Open cannot be decided again.","UC-29"],
["BR-50","The number of sessions a PT teaches per day is decided by the PT when publishing slots; the system sets no limit.","UC-30"],
["BR-51","A PT may publish slots for any future date, without a limit on weeks or months ahead.","UC-30"],
["BR-52","A customer who does not show up has the session deducted: JOB-04 closes it as Missed (CBR-42) and it is never refunded.","UC-31, UC-36"],
["BR-53","For a couple package, deductions are made from the shared quota regardless of who is absent.","UC-31"],
["BR-54",W+"the PT no longer marks absences; JOB-04 closes sessions after the session day (CBR-42). P-07 is withdrawn with it.","—"],
["BR-55",W+"there is no Absent button; a no-show becomes Missed / NoCheckIn through JOB-04.","—"],
["BR-56",W+"replaced by CBR-42 and CBR-67 (a couple session is CheckedIn when either member checked in that day).","—"],
["BR-57","The PT does not approve or reject individual sessions of a confirmed package schedule.","UC-32"],
["BR-58","A PT can edit their own note about a client at any time; saving overwrites the current note."+NI,"UC-33"],
["BR-59","A PT can delete their own note about a client. The note is hidden permanently (soft delete, GBR-05) and the PT can then write a new note for that client."+NI,"UC-33"],
["BR-60","A PT can edit a workout or meal plan they created at any time. Edits to a published plan reach the customer only when the PT publishes again; the customer always sees the latest published version."+NI,"UC-34"],
["BR-61","A PT can delete a workout or meal plan they created. It disappears from the customer's My Plan screen immediately (soft delete, GBR-05), and the PT can then write a new plan of that type for the client."+NI,"UC-34"],
["BR-62",W+"the separate \"swap on behalf of a customer without an account\" option was merged into Reschedule (BR-64); no swap quota is used.","—"],
["BR-63","A PT who cannot teach a session, or whose customer asks to move it, agrees with the customer (Zalo / phone) on one of three options — reschedule, transfer to another PT, or cancel with a cash refund — before acting in the system.","UC-35"],
["BR-64","Reschedule: the session moves to another Free slot of the same PT, from now up to 14 days ahead and not after the package end date; the target must not be held, must not be on a closed day or in a shift covered by the PT's leave request, and must not overlap another session of the customer or partner. A target day without gym access is allowed but marked (CBR-61). An optional note of up to 500 characters can be added. The session stays Scheduled, keeps its commission, is not deducted and does not use any swap quota; the old slot returns to Free; the move is logged as PtReschedule.","UC-35"],
["BR-65","Transfer: the session keeps its date and time and moves to a Free slot of another PT who is Working, whose account is Active and who is free at exactly that time; the receiving PT must not be on leave in that shift. The session stays Scheduled and is not deducted; the PT in charge of the package does not change. The move is logged as PtTransfer and the customer and the receiving PT are notified (CBR-46).","UC-35"],
["BR-66","Cancel: the session becomes Cancelled (ByPt); a reason of 5–500 characters and the tick \"customer agreed to a cash refund\" are mandatory. The slot returns to Free. The system creates no refund transaction.","UC-35"],
["BR-67","The money for a session cancelled under BR-66 is returned to the customer in cash by the PT, outside the system.","UC-35"],
["BR-68","When a session is transferred, the session value is unchanged and nothing is charged or refunded; the commission is recomputed for the receiving PT: round(session value × receiving PT's commission rate ÷ 100).","UC-35"],
["BR-69","A PT who cannot teach a session must handle it in the system (BR-64, BR-65 or BR-66) before the session starts. Violations are dealt with by the Manager outside the system.","UC-35"],
["BR-70","Only the PT in charge of the session may reschedule, transfer or cancel it, and only while it is Scheduled and has not started (otherwise MSG91). The Receptionist and Manager do not act on the PT's behalf. Concurrent changes are serialised: a target slot taken meanwhile is refused (MSG103).","UC-35"],
["BR-71","A session cancelled under BR-66 is still deducted from the package, because the customer has been repaid in cash.","UC-35"],
["BR-72","A customer who cannot use the gym on the chosen date (CBR-117) cannot book a single PT session."+NI,"UC-37"],
["BR-73",W+"customers no longer swap sessions; P-08 is only stored in the subscription (MaxSwapsSnapshot).","—"],
["BR-74",W+"no swap function exists.","—"],
["BR-75",W+"no swap function exists.","—"],
["BR-76",W+"no swap function exists; the customer contacts the PT (BR-63).","—"],
["BR-77",W+"no swap function exists.","—"],
["BR-78",W+"no swap function exists.","—"],
["BR-79",W+"customers no longer cancel sessions (UC-39 withdrawn).","—"],
["BR-80","When a transaction becomes Success the order becomes Paid immediately, provided the order is not Cancelled and the amount equals the amount payable exactly; payment and entitlement are written in the same transaction and a repeated gateway call changes nothing.","UC-PAY"],
# ---- new in v27 ----
["BR-81","Start date of a membership package or day pass: if the customer still holds a membership that has not expired, the new package starts the day after it ends (chained, not selectable); otherwise it starts today or on a date chosen up to 7 days ahead. After an online purchase the customer may move the start date of an unused membership package once, to a date from today to today + 7 days; the end date is recomputed from the package duration.","UC-20, UC-22, UC-41"],
["BR-82","A customer whose profile is Frozen or Inactive cannot create, cancel or pay an online order.","UC-22, UC-PAY"],
["BR-83","The Manager confirms in the system that a transaction on the refund list (CBR-72) has been refunded, entering a note of 5–500 characters (bank account or transfer reference). A transaction can be confirmed only once; the confirmation is audited.","UC-26"],
["BR-84","A new leave request can only be Annual or Unpaid. Sick remains only on historical requests.","UC-14"],
["BR-85","Annual leave uses the yearly quota P-23 minus Approved and Pending annual days. If the remaining quota is smaller than the days requested, the system proposes splitting the request into an Annual part and an Unpaid part; the employee must accept the split, and the balance is re-checked when the request is saved (MSG193, MSG194). One notification is sent for the whole request.","UC-14, UC-15"],
["BR-86","An employee may withdraw their own request while it is Pending; it is removed (GBR-05 exception) and the withdrawal is audited.","UC-14"],
["BR-87","An employee cannot have two requests that are not Rejected for the same date and shift.","UC-14"],
["BR-88","On the Pending tab the Manager may approve several selected requests at once (1–50, current page only). Each request is re-checked and saved in its own transaction; requests that fail a check stay Pending and their reasons are listed, while the others are approved.","UC-15"],
["BR-89","A request whose leave has already started can still be approved, but the Manager must confirm the employee was actually off and give a reason of 5–500 characters; the audit line says \"late approval\".","UC-15"],
["BR-90","Body measurements: one measurement per customer per day — saving again on the same date overwrites it. The date cannot be in the future or before 2000. Weight 20–300 kg and height 100–250 cm are required; body fat 3–70 %, muscle 10–70 % and waist 40–200 cm are optional; note up to 200 characters. The height of the last measurement is pre-filled. Only the customer sees their own measurements; PT measurements at the gym are kept separately.","UC-49"],
["BR-91","BMI = weight ÷ height² (m), computed, never stored, and grouped by the Asian scale: < 18.5 underweight, 18.5–22.9 normal, 23–24.9 overweight, ≥ 25 obese. The screen shows five tiles (weight, BMI, body fat, muscle, waist) with the change since the first measurement, a line chart of one chosen metric over real dates, and the history newest first.","UC-49"],
["BR-92","The customer may delete one of their own measurements after confirmation; it is removed permanently (GBR-05 exception).","UC-49"],
["BR-93","The Exercise Library is a member benefit: a customer may open it when they hold, today, a Membership or PT package whose package has \"Unlocks Exercise Library\" set and whose term covers today (Active or Frozen; a couple partner counts). Otherwise the screen is locked with the reason — never bought, expired on dd/mm, or starts on dd/mm — and lists the packages that unlock it. A PT can always open it. The check is done on the server; typing the URL does not bypass it.","UC-48"],
["BR-94","Exercise Library search: name keyword up to 50 characters, muscle group (8 groups), equipment (12 types), sort by name or \"with image first\"; 12 exercises per page; an unknown value is ignored and the page number is clamped to the valid range. Names stay in English; groups, muscles and equipment are shown in Vietnamese.","UC-48"],
["BR-95","Exercise data come from the public wger API (API-05) and are cached. The cache is refreshed when it is empty or older than 1 day, replacing all rows in one transaction. If wger fails, the old data stay with a notice of the last update and the next attempt is made 5 minutes later; if there is no data at all, an error with a reload action is shown (MSG306). An exercise without a wger image gets an illustration chosen by exercise name or muscle group, labelled as an illustration, without repeating an image on the same page. The wger source and licence (CC BY-SA 4.0) are credited on the page.","UC-48"],
["BR-96","PT sale hold: \"Hold schedule\" creates a Pending counter order and puts every chosen slot on Held for 15 minutes (a fixed value), creating Held slots where the PT had none; other Receptionists and the PT see them as held. Payment is accepted only while the hold is valid. \"Release hold\" (after confirmation) or expiry cancels the order, deletes the slots created by the hold and returns the others to Free; expired holds are released the next time the PT sale screen is used. No voucher can be applied (CBR-76).","UC-21"],
["BR-97","PT slot publishing: new slots are drafts until the PT presses Publish; publishing sends all drafts and removals in one transaction and saves all or nothing. Each new slot must start on a 15-minute mark in the future, lie fully within the opening hours of that date (not a closed day), have length P-06, not overlap a shift covered by the PT's Pending or Approved leave, and not overlap another draft or a published slot. A draft at the start time of a withdrawn slot reopens that slot if the lengths are equal. Publishing with no change is refused (MSG320); if P-06 changed since the page was opened, the PT must reload (MSG321).","UC-30"],
["BR-98","The PT can withdraw only their own Free slots that have not started, have no Scheduled session and are not held; withdrawal sets them to Withdrawn (never deleted). Helpers only prepare drafts: \"Remove all free slots\" of the week, \"Copy week to next week\" (slots that cannot be added are skipped and counted) and a date picker.","UC-30"],
["BR-99","When a PT-sale date uses a time the PT has not opened on that date, the screen marks it \"PT not opened\"; the hold is refused until the Receptionist ticks \"Confirmed with PT\". The system then creates that slot as Held.","UC-21"],
["BR-100","When a PT sale is paid: the order becomes Paid with a Success transaction (cash, or transfer with optional reference up to 50 characters), the subscription is created with session value = round(price ÷ number of sessions) and commission = round(session value × PT commission rate ÷ 100) per session, and the holder, the partner and the PT receive a bell notification.","UC-21"],
["BR-101","My Bookings (view only): lists the customer's PT packages (in progress / ended) and single sessions; for the chosen package it shows the next session, progress, the weekly template (the start time used by at least half of that weekday's sessions, ties → earliest; other sessions are listed as \"different time\" with the move reason), the session strip and the \"watch\" list (upcoming warnings, absences, cancellations). It shows at most one call to action, by priority: buy a membership (an upcoming session without gym access) > buy a PT package at the counter (≥ 3 single sessions in 30 days) > rejoin at the counter (package ended) > renew at the counter (≤ 3 sessions or ≤ 14 days left).","UC-36"],
["BR-102","My PT Sessions (view only): week timetable in three bands by start time — morning (before 13:00), afternoon (13:00–17:59), evening (from 18:00) — or month calendar. Each session shows one of: today, upcoming, needs attention (no gym access, frozen or closed day), result pending (ended, waiting for JOB-04), checked in, missed (with reason), cancelled (with reason). The detail shows the PT, package, status and reason, a Zalo link, copy phone and an \"add to Google Calendar\" link. Customers cannot cancel or move sessions.","UC-36"],
["BR-103","PT schedule week view: each slot is shown as free, held (order awaiting payment), locked (leave pending / approved) or booked; a booked session shows upcoming → in progress → result pending, or its result. A slot can be added from the opening time (rounded up to 15 minutes; today only after the current time) until closing time minus P-06 (rounded down); a closed day accepts no new slot. The grid shows the 13:00 shift divider.","UC-30, UC-32"],
["BR-104","PT dashboard: today's schedule for 7 days (today to today + 6), the \"needs attention\" list for the next 14 days (sessions without gym access, inside a freeze period or on a closed day — with a link to handle the session), the assigned packages with the customer's phone and Zalo link, the monthly result and commission (CheckedIn, Missed by reason, Cancelled; commission from stored amounts) and the weather forecast (API-04).","UC-32"],
["BR-105","Customer dashboard: shows the profile, whether the customer can use the gym today (CBR-117), packages in use or not started, the next 5 PT sessions, up to five warning banners (red: profile Expired, a session on a day without gym access; amber: profile Frozen with the freeze period, membership ending soon unless a chained package exists, a Pending online order awaiting payment), the monthly attendance streak and the 5 latest notifications. It only reads statuses; it never changes them.","UC-41"],
["BR-106","Notification bell: shows the 10 latest notifications of the signed-in account with read / unread state; the user can mark one or all as read. Notifications created by the system have no sender (GBR-15).","UC-50"],
["BR-107","Facilities are managed as groups and items: a facility group has a name (3–100 characters), category, location, unit label (up to 15 characters), image and visibility; each physical equipment item has a code unique in the whole system (2–20 characters, e.g. TM-001), a label unique within its group (1–50 characters, e.g. \"12 kg\"), a placement note (up to 100 characters) and a status Available, UnderMaintenance or Retired. Quantities are computed, never typed: total = items not Retired; available = Available items without an Open or In Progress request; under maintenance = items UnderMaintenance or with such a request.","UC-27"],
["BR-108","Reporting broken equipment is a two-step flow: (1) choose the facility group and one or more of its items — items that are Retired, UnderMaintenance or already have an Open or In Progress request cannot be selected, so an item has at most one open request; (2) enter priority (default Normal), incident type, description (10–500 characters), optional affected-items note (up to 100 characters), whether a warning tag was placed, and optional images. One request (BT-nnnn) is created per item, all in one transaction — if any item is missing or Retired nothing is saved — and every Manager receives one bell notification.","UC-28"],
["BR-109","When deciding a maintenance request the Manager sees the item's last closed request and the availability of its group, may add a note of up to 500 characters and chooses \"Set item to Under maintenance\" (CBR-101). The reporting Receptionist is notified of the approval or rejection; the approving Manager is notified when the request is closed.","UC-29"],
["BR-110","Package catalogue: name 3–50 characters and unique among packages on sale; price 10,000–500,000,000 VND in multiples of 1,000; description up to 255 characters; benefits list; \"Unlocks Exercise Library\". A membership lasts 1, 3, 6, 12, 24 or 36 months, a day pass exactly 1 day, a PT package 1, 3, 6 or 12 months with 1–255 estimated sessions. Single-session packages can be edited but not created. \"Stop selling\" never affects sold packages (CBR-97); selling again requires a unique name and an allowed duration. Saves use a row-version check (MSG22) and are audited.","UC-10"],
["BR-111","Operational report: From and To dates are required, From ≤ To, with no limit on the range; ranges up to 62 days are charted per day, longer ranges per month. The CSV export contains exactly the displayed report (GBR-33). The Admin report adds audit metrics (CBR-103).","UC-46, UC-47"],
["BR-112","Manager leave list: opens on the Pending tab; Pending, Approved and Rejected list requests, All groups requests by employee. Pending requests are ordered with leave starting today or tomorrow first, then by submission time; decided requests by decision time, newest first. Filters: employee name or code, position, leave type and submission date range (empty by default). Clicking a row opens the detail; Approve and Reject (with reason) are also available on the row.","UC-15"],
]
